Z||000000||Kasdan||12-05-2001||08:46 PM||||Black!  I know i said i was going with red and black stripes, but ive decided against it due to the cost of red paint.  black is much cheaper and i liked my black car better.  Im going to go with gloss black paint, silver aero trim, silver side trim, and silver louvers and silver stripes.  what do you guys think?<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-05-2001||08:57 PM||||Having owned a black car in the past (non Fiero), they really do look great when they are all polished up and shiny.  The silver trim will also look sharp.<P>Black, or dark cars in general, show the dust off real well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||12-05-2001||09:06 PM||||If you want it to look good, plan on washing it every week.  Seriously, every week or sooner it needs washed.  With our body design, dust loves to stick behind the window and on the tail section.  Lots of low pressure in those areas...dust settles and there's not much wind or rain to take care of it if the weather's bad either.<P>If you want red, don't worry about the price of paint.  Think how long-term this investment is; don't make a sacrifice that will bite you in the ass for the next eight years or longer.  Also, paint is one of the worst things you can be cheap with.<P>Lastly, silver louvers???  Think of all the crap shooting through your engine louvers.  OK, now think of how easy to clean those louvers are.  You following?  Now realize they were never painted body color from the factory.  Things starting to click yet?  If you did that, you'd clean those so often the paint would start to wear.  Even with powdercoat, they would get dirty so often it would hardly be worth the cool factor.  Just my opinion.<P>I love my black when it's all shiny, but it gets VERY hot and needs cleaned all the time.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*edited typo*<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||1
